      ⍝ regression (Blake McBride, Bugs12.md #2, 2026-08-06): f¨ on an
      ⍝ empty nested array whose (disclosed) prototype item has more
      ⍝ than one element used to build a result with uninitialized
      ⍝ Cells (aborts via Cell::init_other()'s assert, or dispatches a
      ⍝ garbage vtable call with asserts off). ScalarFunction.cc's
      ⍝ do_eval_fill_B() only ever wrote cell 0 of the fill result,
      ⍝ regardless of how many cells the (possibly non-scalar)
      ⍝ prototype item actually needed.
